abstract: >
  A MachineMandate is a selective-disclosure JSON Web Token verifiable
  credential that binds a bounded grant of authority to one exact action
  through an action-hash tamper-seal. It is presented over OpenID for
  Verifiable Presentations to a four-gate verifier that denies
  out-of-mandate actions: credential cryptography, attestation freshness,
  issuer listing in a trusted list, and mandate-constraint enforcement.
  This repository reproduces the gate-ablation table of the accompanying
  preprint from a single command. It is a research artifact: the trust
  anchors are synthetic, the attestation root is a software TPM, and
  nothing here is an eIDAS trust service or carries legal effect.

